{"title":"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Complementary_Counting)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Complementary Counting)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle\" title=\"Angle\">angle</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is chosen at random from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Interval\" title=\"Interval\">interval</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/c/20c42c8048152b5255ec6306912727c82892e18a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0^\\circ &lt; x &lt; 90^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"105\" height=\"13\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the probability that the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/1/a4115fec951b86e383fc70c3b0e2c35e6704f6db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2 x, \\cos^2 x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/d/06dc918f8b7700e8637454c2d98382de60651e06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x \\cos x$\" width=\"76\" height=\"12\" /> are not the lengths of the sides of a triangle. Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/0/470866514bc4d1cd4e5932cd1e01adb4234f9a61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = d/n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the number of degrees in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/0/050e777fcc165b05dd0d082a2b98aba9e6adc30c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{arctan}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"11\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive_integer\" title=\"Positive integer\">positive integers</a> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cd2699a03d1196f40af042cc5ac55c52692e8df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n &lt; 1000,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"113\" height=\"16\" /> find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/0/06042c919364943ac222dc0a083e87e47007e8b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the three expressions are symmetric with respect to interchanging <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb300dacfcde1b57ad070409262b1743e0cd966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5e108fdc4bf4fb6151cb922992f23bc6c35985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos$\" width=\"24\" height=\"8\" />, and so the probability is symmetric around <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8adb649f063149ebc97d3ee58c4fd38d4c440846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />.  Thus, take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/9167e7a81a116e2428c8230cb0f3e05efc821d23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; x &lt; 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"13\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/9/73988ffd3b09c877c3066ba27623c6fb01900d84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x &lt; \\cos x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"97\" height=\"12\" />.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0de76f1bf5f213b9e8868bef1e9481288e317cb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos^2 x$\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" /> is the largest of the three given expressions and those three lengths not forming a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a> is equivalent to a violation of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_inequality\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Triangle inequality\">triangle inequality</a>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/5/e9517416a3c31919329a0da7536cd7ea943ff949.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos^2 x &gt; \\sin^2 x + \\sin x \\cos x\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>This is equivalent to \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/0/d00b48f38038b52b18c0bed05b4995a6adef3920.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos^2 x - \\sin^2 x &gt; \\sin x \\cos x\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>and, using some of our <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trigonometric_identities\" title=\"Trigonometric identities\">trigonometric identities</a>, we can re-write this as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/b/22bbc57442d2171f8ecde9fdc9d6e94039778248.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 2x &gt; \\frac 12 \\sin 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"131\" height=\"37\" />. Since we've chosen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/4/c546e76617fb11b889ffa79020505469446b7411.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in (0, 45)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/c/92ca17a0cebe897b53af88f58e86c2d29e925ef1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 2x &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"79\" height=\"13\" /> so \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/1/f1190e08567586a123631e30e1c61bdeb88563a8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 &gt; \\tan 2x \\Longrightarrow  x &lt; \\frac 12 \\arctan 2.\\]\" width=\"238\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Probability\" title=\"Probability\">probability</a> that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> lies in this range is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/0/880c5b866e2133bcac4f7687b178d7114ba54347.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 1{45} \\cdot \\left(\\frac 12 \\arctan 2\\right) = \\frac{\\arctan 2}{90}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"229\" height=\"43\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/5/865dd25261a2f76b4036ca6b566e0d94c0ffd612.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/4/0e47976b1469a44ad1f7f409fb6195c2a3fcb7bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 90$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> and our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/b/c3be6597eeecab3cc2ac976b20eb5526825a4a33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{092}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Complementary_Counting.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Complementary_Counting)\">Solution 2 (Complementary Counting)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Complementary Counting)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We seek a complementary counting argument, where we look for the probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3dd322af9fa1cc15dc12d18fab5d89e1359ad90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2 x$\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0de76f1bf5f213b9e8868bef1e9481288e317cb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos^2 x$\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/d/06dc918f8b7700e8637454c2d98382de60651e06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x \\cos x$\" width=\"76\" height=\"12\" /> form the side lengths of a triangle.\n</p><p>By the triangle inequality, we must have the following three inequalities to be true: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/a/bba357fec5544abab409f2cb0c3b0d881ec26833.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x &gt; \\sin x \\cos x\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/e/bbe0c97c2cd74851c506630b02621727ab73a77c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin^2 x + \\sin x \\cos x &gt; \\cos^2 x\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/f/85fba6e2d702f21af5a233caa31d3f7b586ae032.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos^2 x + \\sin x \\cos x &gt; \\sin^2 x\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"17\" />\nThe first inequality will always hold since we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/5/a958fb1f7b5b87ef62ed4a2205643ef36cb3df4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"19\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/0/8707ae170a50d534ef3ed76da4417d4e06d142ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 &gt; \\sin x \\cos x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> (The maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/d/06dc918f8b7700e8637454c2d98382de60651e06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x \\cos x$\" width=\"76\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82e05664520bd2aeeea98ef595c0bdaae344f59b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x = \\cos x = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"152\" height=\"43\" />).\n</p><p>Now, we examine the second inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/9/fa92b859e0bd8a41387d166d511eb69d3b165466.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2 x + \\sin x \\cos x &gt; \\cos^2 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"213\" height=\"19\" />. If we subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3dd322af9fa1cc15dc12d18fab5d89e1359ad90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2 x$\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> from both sides, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/f/ccfc6ced7f6dce5fe12d464aef466cc2914449a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x \\cos x &gt; \\cos^2 x - \\sin^2 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"213\" height=\"19\" />. Aha! This resembles our sine and cosine double angle identities. Therefore, our inequality is now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/c/9cc87dcc5bf7b716afb32027fd7cb7d890d73977.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin 2x &gt; 2\\cos 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" />. We can divide both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/1/f01f935e92d5237e2b29debf11c43492b27c18b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 2x$\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" /> and we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/b/86be4d20745183048850a7515cc7192f4a3e4ca7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan 2x &gt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" />.  The solutions to this occur when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/f/4cf377a75cc85d39645510682802dc21ddf9bd7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45 \\geq x &gt; \\frac{\\arctan 2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"146\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>(To understand why it must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/1/4715b1c903cbf77fe76e5adfc949027849bb979c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"31\" height=\"13\" />, we can draw the unit circle, and notice as x moves from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb85664c06d94ff48d244b0b510e6975f03836e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\arctan 2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/8/4d89357bdd19795ccb9fd53b8528e215d4aa860c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan x$\" width=\"39\" height=\"11\" /> approaches <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/7/b671f1bb7e4ee86584347d5d22f1dc8abdb5bef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"9\" />. We must cap <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, since if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/6/3a639a6da86d1b8ceeef973b683ac9e13d667e91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/7/7b72f363443f912989a633aa817374794a102fbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x &gt; 90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"64\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/8/4d89357bdd19795ccb9fd53b8528e215d4aa860c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan x$\" width=\"39\" height=\"11\" /> will be negative.)\n</p><p><br />\nNext, we examine the third inequality, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/0/6b032ce379a33945b38b232cc5a3b01c81959a94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos^2 x + \\sin x \\cos x &gt; \\sin^2 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"213\" height=\"19\" />. Once again, we can get our double angle identities for sine and cosine by subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/c/c2c47a2df5fc9f39345cb77d835d3f56184bfa1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos^2 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"17\" /> from both sides. We have, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8c02842ad083a453445959ff5b44b9acedf4152.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x \\cos x &gt; \\sin^2 x -\\cos^2 x \\to \\sin 2x &gt; -2\\cos 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"384\" height=\"19\" />. \n</p><p>Next, we again, divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/1/f01f935e92d5237e2b29debf11c43492b27c18b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 2x$\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" /> to produce a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/8/46809f2ea559cc16a5f5d557ae890f61508de8fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> (we do this because one trig function is easier to deal with than 2). However, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/c/92ca17a0cebe897b53af88f58e86c2d29e925ef1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 2x &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"79\" height=\"13\" />, we do not need to flip the sign since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/9/ec9f5b656042780e5a3f142ba9a895264289ace5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin 2x &gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" />, and so if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/56318254400ef34fb2fcd7cd221a5e1c0ca4ce7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 2x &gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" />, all values for which that is true satisfy the inequality. So we only consider if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/4/fb4165e873a281f84b08ad3d81506432b8eba915.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 2x &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" />, and when we divide by a negative, we must flip the sign. Thus we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/e/3bee9301248a6ed31658c4e5723106e461f08a73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan 2x &lt; -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"98\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>We can take the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3bed2a11e55445f027f026c415d1867fc7ec32d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\arctan$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" /> of both sides, and we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/7/357cbb9b6f49babd3c69643c2c0a7db0ee52d4a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\arctan -2}{2}&gt; x \\geq 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"160\" height=\"38\" />. Once again, to better understand this, we can draw the angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c655c68914e54e45660d3e2634437850114315b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan 2x = -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"98\" height=\"15\" />, and we notice as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> moves to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/9/3399eca2cdd9e0a8e37a5b1ce496e0dec7cafe59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/8/46809f2ea559cc16a5f5d557ae890f61508de8fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> approaches <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/2/1b2265075c3259b3dc4adbefa0633111915dd0d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$- \\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"31\" height=\"9\" />. We must cap <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> since if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/7/a7797737765dc498497015320be287bb55e5ef3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/f/96fe48a41f673c1de4f07853fc8190c8cd1bb3f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan 2x &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>Notice that if we draw the terminal points for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb85664c06d94ff48d244b0b510e6975f03836e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\arctan 2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/f/0afe012da09053391b3e43bf7c7b2c4f76937f83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\arctan -2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"38\" />, they have the same smaller angle with the x and y axis respectively. This means the range of degree measures for which our inequalities hold is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/9/a396100508509595323fcc7214457fa0d8613984.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90 - \\frac{\\arctan 2}{2} &gt; x &gt; \\frac{\\arctan 2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"234\" height=\"38\" /> which has an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/7/2b75beea926933101cbf19b41c992bd7d52e2cb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90 - \\arctan 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" />. However, we want the complement of this, which has an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/c/28c9180b0859ecd8c1ed0eb7c3f65ed1e156dcc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90 - (90 - \\arctan 2) = \\arctan 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"246\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore, the desired probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/9/ec953dc0eee81389054b7aa6ae8f7ad500aac574.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\arctan2}{90}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b70ec15a32e3ef5d30dee80c1120bb004657fee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n=2+90=92$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"167\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>-BossLu99\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I\" title=\"2003 AIME I\">2003 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2003\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017201348\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.051 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.072 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 525/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1790/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 112/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 15864/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.510      1 -total\n 59.81%    8.081      1 Template:AIME_box\n 37.89%    5.119      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3088:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017201348 and revision id 220895. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}